WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
This can't be!

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:05.620
There has never been a great white in these warm tropical waters before!

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.780
Never! This is more than a coincidence.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.900
This shark appears to be possessed, as if it's hunting you down, like it's personal.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:39.920
Jaws. And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.140
I'm Mike.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.640
I'm Joe. I'm Sean.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.220
And I'm Sam. Guys, today we're talking about Jaws.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.600
Wow. Has anybody seen the movie?

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.260
I've seen the movie.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.480
I joke, I joke. Not in a very long time, actually.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.660
I really don't remember much about it.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.840
I have not seen the movie.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:56.820
Ever. No.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.580
What about anything from Steven Spielberg?

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.280
I've seen a lot of scenes from the movie.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:07.160
Okay. Yeah. What was the movie that Steven Spielberg made before this one that was like a truck chasing a car?

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:12.120
Uh, Cars. Yeah, before Pixar remade it.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.460
No, no, no, no.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:14.500
There was a movie.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.020
Duel. Duel?

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.760
Yes, you've got to check this out.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.880
Never seen Duel.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:25.680
Yeah, uninformed people who don't know what Duel is, you will not believe that Steven Spielberg made a movie like that

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.580
and then went on to make movies like this.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.840
Interesting. It's literally just a truck chasing a car for like two hours.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.760
So Duel was really good. Jaws was really bad.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.500
Jaws is, well they're both essentially things chasing people.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.680
Yeah, that's true. Jaws is a spiritual sequel.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.660
But then people chase things at the end of Jaws.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.940
Yes, that's true. Oh, sorry.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:50.020
Spoiler alert. It's amazing how much of like the movie Jaws people associate with the beach.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.920
When like that's just one scene in the movie pretty much.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:59.780
But it's also like that they want the, it's basically just the mayor saying we want the beach to stay open.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.820
That's the entire like crux of the movie.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:14.360
Yeah, I guess. My thing with Jaws in general is that this movie, not that scary to me growing up like 20 years later than the movie.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.800
What was the, no. It scared the hell out of the movie, right?

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:18.720
Yeah, it's the 80s. Okay, I just wasn't sure.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.200
Or 70s I think. It was 80s.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.400
No, I think it was.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.360
You're right. This is 76 or something.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.480
Yeah. I don't know why I think.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.920
Yeah, but I'm saying like 20 years later it wasn't that scary to me.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:33.040
But then I finally went to Universal Studios and went on the, no, yeah, and went on the Jaws ride.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.500
I went on the Jaws ride where you're like in the boat.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.680
Yeah. And then all of a sudden the water goes on fire.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:43.380
And that was the first time in my life that I learned that like water can turn on fire.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.100
And I was like, what? There's oil in it or something?

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.180
I was like water is supposed to protect us.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.280
Water cannot turn on fire.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.520
There can be oil on water.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.580
That's what you thought though. Yes, but you get what I'm saying is like I always thought water was the great protector of fire.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:00.300
And then I was like, wait, fire can set water?

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.360
Yeah, I was like that's dangerous.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.380
It just changed your world view.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.460
It really did. I just remember that sticking with me.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.260
More than anything else in Universal Studios.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.880
If water is not safe. Yeah, exactly.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.080
What is? Turns out the fire wasn't even the worst part of the ride though.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.320
Because then there's that mechanical Jaws that like comes out and bites the ship up and stuff like that.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.320
That's the sound he made.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:19.920
Did you do the voice acting?

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.580
Yeah, it's actually more of like, it's like a quack.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.380
It's like, mwah. It's like a Waluigi thing.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.320
Yeah, it's a Waluigi voice.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:30.000
And then of course, Jaws 3D in Back to the Future 2.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.520
That was great.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.440
That's like the first, it's sad.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.000
That's like the thing I think of first.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.220
Wow. The Back to the Future reference.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.460
The 2015 film.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:38.700
I mean I saw Jaws when I was like a kid.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.740
I really don't remember it.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.340
Okay. You remember the music.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.720
Oh, of course. How does it go?

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:46.480
Over and over again.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:47.560
Okay, cool. That's good.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.380
I thought you were going to keep going.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:58.240
Since we're sharing like moments from our childhood and stuff, I will say that for me the Jaws theme and the James Bond theme can work into one.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.760
It kind of goes like...

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.200
Oh, what if Jaws was a secret agent?

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.700
Well, Jaws is like a bad guy in the James Bond universe.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.180
But if we're going into things from our childhood,

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.760
I do know that there was a time in my house

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.120
that I thought that there was a guy in my basement

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.300
that was like a monster

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.600
and that he was going to eat me.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.640
His name was Kilio.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.780
Okay. Wait a minute, but this has nothing to do with Jaws.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.240
We're talking about Jaws.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.540
He's getting there. Oh, I thought you were just talking about things from our childhood.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:41.580
No, no, no, no. It's fine.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.420
Any other thoughts about the movie before we go into the game?

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:47.680
My basement growing up.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.800
No, no, no.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:49.980
It's fine. You didn't even see the movie.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:50.860
You can't have thoughts.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.300
I had a basement, though.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.920
You don't have to speak until we talk about the game.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:55.940
There were lots of spiders in the basement,

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:56.840
so I didn't really go there.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.560
Okay. Anyway, long story short,

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.040
the movie is still worth watching today.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.000
I'll uphold to that.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.880
I will say that this is a movie that's going to be good for a long time.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.460
As long as there are sharks in our ocean,

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:07.500
which could be maybe another 10, 15 years tops.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.000
By the time this airs, they may not be.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.340
Yeah. So as long as there are sharks in our ocean,

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.960
Jaws is a very relatable story.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.320
I think that's why you're asking about why everyone thinks of the beach scene.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.700
Because that's like what everyone else,

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:20.620
like everyone goes to the beach.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:22.500
Not everyone hunts sharks.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.960
Well, yeah, exactly. I don't.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.740
That was Steven Spielberg's acceptance speech for the movie

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.320
when it was just, you know,

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:33.140
like the award for anything goes to Jaws.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.260
He would just get them and be like,

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:37.700
that was one of the motifs of the movie was that this could happen to anyone.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.820
Yeah. None of that was true.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.120
Jaws didn't even win awards.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:44.280
One of the motifs of the movie was sharks.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.500
It's time to talk about gameplay.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.840
It's specifically time to talk about first impressions.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.860
I would like to say that this is our first time playing the Jaws game, correct?

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.200
Yes. Any of us? This is a pretty popular NES game.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.580
A lot of people played this because they loved the movie so much

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:03.160
that they figured, oh, I should probably get the great video game that goes alongside it.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.780
Anyway, Sam, first impressions?

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:07.200
So my first impression was that I thought it was cool

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.800
how there was an overworld,

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.180
and I kind of wanted to see how that would play out.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:15.480
I didn't really understand why the boat would just kind of stop sometimes

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:18.120
and then toss me out of it and make me have to swim.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.380
But, you know, I thought it was pretty cool,

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.000
and I really liked the overworld song.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.060
I thought it really gave a nice vibe.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:29.320
My first impression was also I was interested by all the different stages

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.520
that you would find yourself in.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:37.580
But then I was quickly, I wasn't as impressed when it turns out

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:41.200
that the overworld is literally just two screens wide,

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:46.140
and you just sort of float back and forth between two little towns.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:49.560
So I was just very confused by the whole thing,

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:52.820
and that would continue on into deeper impressions.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:59.260
So my first thought originally was the way that the art style looked.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:03.100
I thought it was a pretty polished-looking game.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.000
And the other big thing that kind of caught my attention

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.720
once I kind of got to figure out what I was going to be doing in this game

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:13.280
was that it's kind of cool, at least a cool idea,

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.660
that you're trying to, we haven't got into this yet,

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.760
but the way you're playing is trying to level up

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.680
to be strong enough to take on Jaws.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.540
So I thought that was cool and different.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:25.320
We haven't really done anything like that too much yet, or at all.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:27.040
And my first impression,

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.780
after we got through the whole overworld and everything like that,

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:33.900
is just when did the Jaws franchise

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.600
become about collecting seashells to get stronger?

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:44.140
And also, when did anybody in Jaws ever fight Stingrays?

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.160
That's true.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.940
Yeah. I feel like that's just the gamified part of it.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.460
I know. I'm sorry, but it's taken me out of it

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:56.320
because you kill so many Stingrays and so many jellyfish

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.960
and only like maybe four to five sharks that aren't even named Jaws.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.980
And then you kill one Jaws.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:05.360
Yeah, it seems like we're the monsters here, really.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.660
One Jaws. You know, when you think about, I mean, what,

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:11.060
Jaws killed two people or three people in the movie?

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:15.100
This is just about wrecking havoc on an ecosystem.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.020
Yeah, and that's kind of what I want to get at,

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.060
but we're going to work our way through that.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:22.220
But I think that was just the most surprising thing to me

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:24.220
was like, this is the gameplay loop they came up with?

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:26.260
It is funny. You literally bomb like jellyfish.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.860
Like you're flying over in the sky.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.440
With deep sea charges.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.620
We're a little overkill there.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:35.800
They barely have like any kind of system of living, you know?

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:38.820
And also like apparently this is just that one town

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:42.520
that all they eat ever is Stingray and jellyfish

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:44.140
because they couldn't think of one other,

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.600
like where is anything else, right?

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:46.720
You wouldn't kill dolphin.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.760
You would. But they would be in that ocean.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.080
Well, there's crabs.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.360
No, but the crabs are like a bone.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.260
Oh, because you can eat crabs.

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:55.620
Yeah, but they... You wonder why.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.800
You just swim down on the bottom and just bite into a crab.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.840
Well, yeah. You should have had to at least pull out like a crab cage.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.860
You just walk up to these crabs and collect them.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.540
That's unrealistic. Maybe they should have just turned into crab cage.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.820
I hadn't thought of the fact that this is unrealistic.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.200
This game couldn't happen anymore.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.200
I just want to know where everybody else is.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:14.540
How is the ocean so blank?

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.600
You could pick up a crab for sure.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.140
With your hands? Yeah.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.580
Easy. And then he bites your nose.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:21.620
Oh, you don't know that.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.780
No. You wouldn't call it a bite of each other.

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:26.080
Just hold his arms. He clamps.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:34.380
Yeah. I just want to talk about the manual for a second because the manual had a pretty fierce

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:40.460
introduction to Jaws that I think I wound up also reading as part of our Back to the Box.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:43.580
You guys decide because I read both openings.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:47.260
But it has like this whole thing of like, you know, the introduction.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:49.260
Similar to how the Goonies do it a really nice setup.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:51.840
So it has that whole, this can't be.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:55.120
There's never been a great white in these warm tropical waters before.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:10:01.360
And then it's like, will you use the mini sub, seaplane, sailboat, or just scuba gear?

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:02.420
It's like, you don't get a choice.

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:03.840
You always turn the boat.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.660
Yeah. And you also have to use all of those things.

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:10.180
And then they say, perhaps it won't even matter.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:12.320
It's got to matter, right?

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.800
Like, it matters what you use.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.600
No, that's like a fatalist idea.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.100
Like, it won't matter because he's always going to best you.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:25.240
Yeah, I guess. Yeah, because then that follows up with, remember, this is some kind of unbelievably powerful eating

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:26.860
machine you're dealing with.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:32.440
Quick, grab your weapons, pack your explosives, and check your maps.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:35.200
Maps. I guess that's the overworld.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.240
Yeah, there's like one. That's two screens.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:39.080
There's no map.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:40.300
You could get lost, though.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:47.820
It's just it. This is the ultimate Jaws challenge because this time it's not over until the only one

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.560
of you is left alive.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.680
Until the only one of you?

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:52.680
Until only one of you.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.920
Oh, I thought it was. Sorry.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.460
No, no, that's my mistake.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:11:00.420
I don't know. I think that it's setting up a game that's much more exciting than what we're about to

