get into. But that's just me.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.420
Maybe I'm projecting. Can we talk?

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.240
Like, were you guys excited playing this game?

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.260
Were you like, oh, I'm hunting for Jaws?

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:17.480
I wouldn't say that I was excited because I'm never very excited about tie-in games, even

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.940
though this isn't so much a tie-in because it came out almost a decade before the game

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:22.840
came out.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:30.140
But when it comes to games made based on movies, I'm never too excited of what to expect because

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:39.520
they're either going to be like sort of cookie cutter games that are based off a very basic

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:44.200
premise. Like, they'll be just a regular shooter or just a beat-em-up or something.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:48.920
Or they can go into weird directions like this one kind of did.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:55.720
So I wasn't excited, but I guess I enjoyed the amount of weirdness that it sort of introduced.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.780
I was kind of excited, like I said, in my initial impression.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:05.220
Once I realized what you were going to be doing, I thought there was a lot of really

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:08.820
cool ideas that we hadn't had before.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:15.120
And just the idea of kind of building yourself up and going through this world map and doing

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:19.920
different, almost like making yourself stronger by collecting different things and whatnot

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.260
sounded very cool to me and kind of satisfying.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:28.820
And unfortunately, I feel like it just never got quite to what I was hoping it was going

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:33.920
to be. No, kind of going off what Sean was saying, I think that whenever we get like a movie title

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:40.080
as a game, there's kind of like the cynic in me is thinking they just have a movie because

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.340
they know that people will buy it.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:42.900
And so it can just be empty content.

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:44.700
But at the same time, I'm also curious.

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:50.520
I was curious just to know how they would have like an extreme fishing game, you know, how

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:53.640
they could make that into something based on a movie.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:55.360
So I was curious. And sharks are cool.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.840
So I, you know, I thought maybe there could be some cool stuff in there.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:00.500
The best part of this game is Jaws himself.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:05.240
